Z||000000||bHooper||05-10-2001||06:28 PM||||i have noticed some very peculiar sounds, from my 5spd GT, lately.<P>first, it seems to make a <I>dingk</I> sound when i put it into reverse, or first gear (at start).  what is that?  could it be the throw out bearing?  i put a new clutch and a used tranny in about 6000 miles ago (i think the tranny had over 120,000 miles on it).<P>secondly, i notice a sound when i accelerate.  its kinda like "small bolts in a glass jar" with some white noise thrown in.  i cant really describe it.  it happens under acceleration; most noticable in 1st and 2nd gear... but can be heard through the higher gears.<P>i suspect that the drivers side CV joint is going bad... but wouldnt this be a ticking only sound?<P>thanks!<P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR>Red '86 GT<BR>KYB's, Eibach's<BR>and spellcheck crash's windows<BR>Poly Bushings<BR>Accel Coil||||reg||5
Z||000001||Kerri 98||05-10-2001||07:51 PM||||The "bolts in a jar" sound could be the timing, have you checked that?||||reg||6
