Z||000003||Mark||05-10-2001||09:34 PM||||I'm thinkin' that "dingk" could be a bad mount somewhere (like dogbone or tranny) since you hear it when the engine/tranny torques over one way or the other.  The excess movement could be causing almost anything to make the noise, like the exhaust).||||reg||1
Z||000004||bHooper||05-10-2001||09:56 PM||||i also have a silent cup of bolts, on my shelf... how bout that?!<P>seriously, all the mounts have been replaced in the last year, so i doubt that could be the problem.<P>i forgot to say, that when i got home, i popped the rear deck and raced the throttle (with the car in neutral of course) and i thought that i lightly heard the "jar" sound.<P>also, i did notice that the car was difficult to put into first gear, at one point today.  but honestly, the car drives great... especially after putting the redline MTL tranny fluid in it!||||reg||1
